From: FrOSCon 2026 MicroVM Project <froscon@example.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 08:35:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pve-docs: Document QEMU microvm machine type in qm.adoc

Add documentation for the lightweight 'microvm' machine type to the
Proxmox VE reference documentation (qm.adoc), explaining its use cases,
virtio-mmio transport, and direct kernel boot capabilities.

---
 qm.adoc | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/qm.adoc b/qm.adoc
index 8e41bf1..a912dc3 100644
--- a/qm.adoc
+++ b/qm.adoc
@@ -210,6 +210,14 @@ QEMU can virtualize different machine types:
   modern guest operating systems, PCIe devices, and PCI passthrough.
   Recommended for modern Linux and Windows setups.
 
+* `microvm`: A minimalist, lightweight x86_64 machine type that omits legacy
+  PCI, ACPI, and BIOS emulation. It relies on `virtio-mmio` transport and direct
+  kernel booting (`-kernel` and `-initrd`/`-append`), enabling sub-second cold
+  boot times and low memory footprints. Recommended for ephemeral workloads,
+  CI/CD runners, and secure multi-tenant microVM sandboxes. Note: microVMs do
+  not support live migration, hardware hotplug, or traditional PCI/PCIe devices.
+
 * `virt` (arm64/aarch64 only): The standard ARM64 virtual machine type.
 
 
